{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7277827","formula":"C₂₂H₂₅NO₂","hill":"C22H25NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":22.0,"H":25.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"RTI-120"},"descriptions":{"en":"RTI-120 ((–)-2β-carbophenoxy-3β-(p-tolyl)tropane or RTI-4229-120) is a phenyltropane derivative which acts as a reasonably selective dopamine reuptake inhibitor, along with weaker inhibition of noradrenaline and serotonin reuptake. It has a reasonably fast rate of occupancy of dopamine transporters in the brain, though slower than that of cocaine itself. RTI-120 has a short duration of action, along with other p-methyl substituted phenyltropanes such as RTI-150, RTI-171 and RTI-199, giving it a more similar pharmacological profile to cocaine compared to longer acting analogues like RTI-121 and RTI-177."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":10109793,"mass":335.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=CC=C(C=C1)C2CC3CCC(C2C(=O)OC4=CC=CC=C4)N3C","inchikey":"HIQHQNWJRSNELD-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"phenyl 8-methyl-3-(4-methylphenyl)-8-azabicyclo[3.2.1]octane-2-carboxylate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"10109793","atoms":50,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.711,"y":0.512,"z":0.885,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.052,"y":0.301,"z":-1.352,"el":"O"},{"x":1.931,"y":2.83,"z":0.974,"el":"N"},{"x":0.626,"y":2.515,"z":0.359,"el":"C"},{"x":2.879,"y":2.569,"z":-0.124,"el":"C"},{"x":0.531,"y":0.969,"z":0.343,"el":"C"},{"x":1.673,"y":0.319,"z":-0.482,"el":"C"},{"x":3.024,"y":1.036,"z":-0.228,"el":"C"},{"x":0.715,"y":3.133,"z":-1.045,"el":"C"},{"x":2.209,"y":3.164,"z":-1.365,"el":"C"},{"x":1.791,"y":-1.18,"z":-0.256,"el":"C"},{"x":2.006,"y":4.201,"z":1.472,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.816,"y":0.554,"z":-0.178,"el":"C"},{"x":1.595,"y":-2.057,"z":-1.32,"el":"C"},{"x":2.093,"y":-1.667,"z":1.012,"el":"C"},{"x":1.703,"y":